{
  "dom_id": "step-e14326",
  "name": "Example: Finding the Product of Two Binomials With Leading Coefficients",
  "problem": "Expand $(5x - 4)(5x + 4) .$",
  "worked_solution": "We will use the difference of square formula:\n\n$$\n(a + b)(a - b) = a^2 - b^2\n$$\n\nSubstituting $a=5x$ and $b=4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t(5x - 4)(5x + 4) &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t(5x)^2 - (4)^2 &= \\[5pt]\n\t\t25x^2 - 16.\n\t}\n$$",
